  "asr_text": "I stood motionless. For an hour he sat in bed, listening. At last, he groaned softly. Not pain, terror. I knew that sound. I uncovered the lantern. Its narrow beam found the eye, wide open. A low, quick beating reached me, like a watch wrapped in cotton. His heart! Faster it went and louder. What if a neighbor heard? I rushed forward. He shrieked once. I dragged him down and pulled the heavy bed over him. Finally, the beating stopped. I checked his pulse. Nothing. I hid his body beneath three floorboards and fitted them back exactly. Not a mark. You could have searched all night. At four in the morning, three police officers knocked. A neighbor had heard a shriek.",
